{"content_hash": "a3ab8fcd3a340d60", "version_id": 207, "article_id": 21, "level_code": "ja_n4", "lang": "ja", "level": 2, "level_label": "N4 初級", "title": "スペインの87歳の女性が亡くなりました 家を追い出された問題で", "title_zh": "西班牙87岁老太太去世，因被赶出家门引发全国抗议", "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6e3x21ev9wwo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/d9ee/live/06010330-c283-11f1-98ea-35e6bf307fc9.jpg", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 381, "reading_minutes": 1.2, "lead": "スペインで、家を追い出された87歳の女性が亡くなりました。この問題で、スペインでは多くの人が protest しています。", "lead_zh": "在西班牙，一位被赶出家门的87岁老太太去世了。因为这件事，西班牙很多人都在抗议。", "preview": "スペインのマドリードで、87歳のマリカルメン・アバスカルさんが亡くなりました。彼女は9月23日、家賃が上がって払えなくなり、家を追い出されました。70年以上住んでいた家でした。", "preview_zh": "在西班牙马德里，87岁的玛里卡门·阿巴斯卡去世了。9月23日，因为房租上涨付不起，她被赶出了家门。那是她住了70多年的家。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 197, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ab49ecc/content/audio/21/ja_n4.mp3", "duration": 78.688, "size_bytes": 475920, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 249, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ab49ecc/content/data/versions/207.json", "paragraphs": ["スペインのマドリードで、87歳のマリカルメン・アバスカルさんが亡くなりました。彼女は9月23日、家賃が上がって払えなくなり、家を追い出されました。70年以上住んでいた家でした。", "アバスカルさんの家を追い出すことは、スペインの住宅問題についての大きな抗議を起こしました。マドリードのテナント組合は「彼女の状況はこの国の歴史の転換点になった」と言いました。", "多くの人がマドリードのプエルタ・デル・ソル広場に集まりました。彼女の死を聞いて、皆で静かに祈りました。ろうそくをたくさんともし、彼女を記念しました。", "人々は「もう一つの追い出しも許さない」「戦いは続く」と叫びました。そして、議会の近くまで歩きました。警察は道をふさぎましたが、大きな問題にはなりませんでした。", "スペインの首相ペドロ・サンチェスさんは、11月29日に選挙をすると言いました。住宅のための法律が議会で反対されたからです。スペインでは住宅問題が大きな政治の問題になっています。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["在西班牙马德里，87岁的玛里卡门·阿巴斯卡去世了。9月23日，因为房租上涨付不起，她被赶出了家门。那是她住了70多年的家。", "把阿巴斯卡赶出家门这件事，引发了关于西班牙住房问题的大规模抗议。马德里租户联盟说：“她的情况成了这个国家历史的转折点。”", "很多人聚集在马德里的太阳门广场。听到她去世的消息，大家一起安静地祈祷。他们点了很多蜡烛来纪念她。", "人们喊着“再也不许赶走任何一个人”“斗争会继续”。然后他们走到了议会附近。警察挡住了路，但没有发生大问题。", "西班牙首相佩德罗·桑切斯说，将在11月29日举行选举。因为住房法案在议会遭到反对。在西班牙，住房问题已经成了很大的政治问题。"], "body": "スペインのマドリードで、87歳のマリカルメン・アバスカルさんが亡くなりました。彼女は9月23日、家賃が上がって払えなくなり、家を追い出されました。70年以上住んでいた家でした。\n\nアバスカルさんの家を追い出すことは、スペインの住宅問題についての大きな抗議を起こしました。マドリードのテナント組合は「彼女の状況はこの国の歴史の転換点になった」と言いました。\n\n多くの人がマドリードのプエルタ・デル・ソル広場に集まりました。彼女の死を聞いて、皆で静かに祈りました。ろうそくをたくさんともし、彼女を記念しました。\n\n人々は「もう一つの追い出しも許さない」「戦いは続く」と叫びました。そして、議会の近くまで歩きました。警察は道をふさぎましたが、大きな問題にはなりませんでした。\n\nスペインの首相ペドロ・サンチェスさんは、11月29日に選挙をすると言いました。住宅のための法律が議会で反対されたからです。スペインでは住宅問題が大きな政治の問題になっています。", "body_zh": "在西班牙马德里，87岁的玛里卡门·阿巴斯卡去世了。9月23日，因为房租上涨付不起，她被赶出了家门。那是她住了70多年的家。\n\n把阿巴斯卡赶出家门这件事，引发了关于西班牙住房问题的大规模抗议。马德里租户联盟说：“她的情况成了这个国家历史的转折点。”\n\n很多人聚集在马德里的太阳门广场。听到她去世的消息，大家一起安静地祈祷。他们点了很多蜡烛来纪念她。\n\n人们喊着“再也不许赶走任何一个人”“斗争会继续”。然后他们走到了议会附近。警察挡住了路，但没有发生大问题。\n\n西班牙首相佩德罗·桑切斯说，将在11月29日举行选举。因为住房法案在议会遭到反对。在西班牙，住房问题已经成了很大的政治问题。", "text": "スペインのマドリードで、87歳のマリカルメン・アバスカルさんが亡くなりました。彼女は9月23日、家賃が上がって払えなくなり、家を追い出されました。70年以上住んでいた家でした。 アバスカルさんの家を追い出すことは、スペインの住宅問題についての大きな抗議を起こしました。マドリードのテナント組合は「彼女の状況はこの国の歴史の転換点になった」と言いました。 多くの人がマドリードのプエルタ・デル・ソル広場に集まりました。彼女の死を聞いて、皆で静かに祈りました。ろうそくをたくさんともし、彼女を記念しました。 人々は「もう一つの追い出しも許さない」「戦いは続く」と叫びました。そして、議会の近くまで歩きました。警察は道をふさぎましたが、大きな問題にはなりませんでした。 スペインの首相ペドロ・サンチェスさんは、11月29日に選挙をすると言いました。住宅のための法律が議会で反対されたからです。スペインでは住宅問題が大きな政治の問題になっています。", "vocab": [{"word": "家賃", "pos": "noun", "zh": "房租", "note": "家賃が上がる＝房租上涨"}, {"word": "追い出す", "pos": "verb", "zh": "赶出，驱逐", "note": "家を追い出される＝被赶出家门"}, {"word": "抗議", "pos": "noun", "zh": "抗议", "note": "抗議する＝抗议"}, {"word": "亡くなる", "pos": "verb", "zh": "去世", "note": "比「死ぬ」更礼貌的说法"}, {"word": "組合", "pos": "noun", "zh": "工会，联盟", "note": "テナント組合＝租户联盟"}, {"word": "広場", "pos": "noun", "zh": "广场", "note": "プエルタ・デル・ソル広場＝太阳门广场"}, {"word": "ろうそく", "pos": "noun", "zh": "蜡烛", "note": "ろうそくをともす＝点蜡烛"}, {"word": "叫ぶ", "pos": "verb", "zh": "喊，叫", "note": "抗議で叫ぶ＝在抗议中喊叫"}, {"word": "首相", "pos": "noun", "zh": "首相", "note": "スペインの首相＝西班牙首相"}, {"word": "選挙", "pos": "noun", "zh": "选举", "note": "選挙をする＝举行选举"}], "title_original": "Spanish pensioner whose eviction sparked nationwide protests dies, union says", "summary_original": "Maricarmen Abascal, 87, was forcibly removed on a stretcher from her apartment of more than 70 years in September.", "body_original": "Spanish pensioner whose eviction sparked nationwide protests dies, union says\nBy\nAlys Davies\nand\nAlba Morgade in Madrid\nPublished\n7 October 2026\nUpdated 59 minutes ago\nAn elderly woman whose eviction sparked nationwide protests over Spain's housing crisis and a political row that triggered early elections has died, according to Madrid's tenants union.\nMaricarmen Abascal, 87, was forcibly removed on a stretcher from her apartment of more than 70 years on 23 September after she was unable to afford rent increases.\nThe company that owned the flat later offered to allow her to return at a lower rate - but she was unable to sign an agreement as she had been admitted to hospital.\n\"We regret to announce that Maricarmen passed away today,\" the Madrid Tenants' Union said in a statement, adding her situation marked \"a turning point in the history of this country\".\nUnion spokesperson Alicia del Río said: \"Speculation costs lives, and today rentierism has finished killing our colleague Maricarmen\" but \"her memory lives on with us\".\nA cause of death was not announced.\nAbascal's death was received in Puerta del Sol with a big collective gasp, then followed by a minute of silence.\nIt is in this square in the centre of Madrid where thousands have been camping since Abascal's eviction last month to demand more affordable housing.\nOn Wednesday, it became the place to pay tribute to her.\nPeople lit dozens of candles around the square in a small improvised vigil that glowed with a warm light on a dry and warm autumn night.\nOther candles formed an altar to Abascal in front of the headquarters of the Community of Madrid government.\nMessages on cardboard banners next to the candles read \"it's not a death, it's a killing\", \"the fight will continue\" and \"Mari Carmen, the grandmother of the whole country\", among others.\nA few hundred people then took to the streets that connect Puerta del Sol with the Spanish Congress, just 500m away, in an improvised protest.\nDuring the march people chanted: \"We will not tolerate a single eviction more\" and \"the fight will continue, Mari Carmen is still alive\". There were other chants against fascism and against the police.\nThe police had set up barriers to block the march. There was not a big police presence, and there was the tension that protests sometimes have.\nMany protesters seemed to feel the police have been complicit in the evictions, as under court orders they have to remove tenants who have been served eviction notices.\nAfter a couple of hours, the chants near Congress gave way to another minute of silence. Then, a big collective shout of \"murderers\".\nWednesday night's march has finished, but the camping, already on its 12th night, will continue \"as long as necessary\" one of the protesters told the BBC.\nAbascal became a symbol for Spain's housing crisis following her eviction.\nHer father first rented the property in 1956 and she continued as the tenant after her parents died, during which time there was a cap on the rent.\nHowever, Urbagestión, which bought the property in 2018, increased the rent from €500 per month (£428; $572) to €2,650 (£2,280; $3,020).\nThe company later offered to reduce this to €1,650 - still €300 more than Abascal's monthly pension.\nThree previous attempts to evict her were blocked by the courts and the case has received increasing media attention.\nAnger over the situation grew, leading to protests and putting pressure on the coalition government to approve emergency housing legislation -\nbut it was rejected in Congress last week\n.\nThat led to further protests,\nwith tens of thousands of people taking\nto the streets\nin cities across the country over the weekend.\nReferring to the rejected bills, the Madrid Tenants' Union said: \"While a historic agreement was reached that would have allowed her to return to her home, this solution has come too late. An absolutely avoidable situation after a torturing process.\"\nIt said the events surrounding her eviction represented a turning point in the country's history, but added that the cost to get to this point had been \"too high\".\n\"Above all, we will fulfil what she always asked of us: 'fight, keep fighting for what is yours',\" it said.\nIn a video recorded from her hospital bed following her eviction, Maricarmen said: \"I haven't managed to defend my home, but I have fought so that others can learn to fight for what's theirs.\"\n\"All my love goes to Maricarmen's family and loved ones,\" Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez said. \"A hug as well to everyone who today feels this loss as their own.\"\nOpposition People's Party leader Alberto Núñez Feijóo also sent his condolences to Maricarmen's loved ones, as he said on X: \"No campaign, no parties, no self-interested exploitation. No more stones in the wall.\n\"In the face of a person's death, only respect is in order,\" he added.\nEarlier on Wednesday, unions had called a general strike to take place on 11 November, demanding housing reforms.\nThe public outcry over Abascal's situation has led to political turmoil in Spain.\nOn Monday Sánchez, who leads a leftist coalition that does not hold a majority in parliament, called an early election for 29 November. It followed his failure to get the emergency housing legislation through Congress.\nThe political right had argued that the government's attempt to intervene in the housing market would have led to fewer homes being rented and would have raised prices further.\nSpeaking on Monday, Sánchez said he needed \"a broader progressive majority\" that can \"overcome the resistance of the elites\" to push through reforms.\nOther issues not relating to housing, such as numerous corruption scandals linked to his party, and pressures relating to the cost of living and immigration, have also caused him problems.\nMost opinion polls suggest the conservatives are likely to emerge as the largest party in the next election. However, they would be expected to need the support of the hard-right Vox party to form a government.\nAdditional reporting by Tom McArthur\nRelated topics\nSpain\nMore on this story\nSpanish PM Sánchez calls early election after housing protests\nPublished\n2 days ago\nDramatic eviction of woman aged 87 highlights Spain's housing shortage\nPublished\n23 September", "fetched_at": "2026-10-08T01:16:22.071120", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "スペイン", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.6, "sm": 125, "em": 600, "cs": 0, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "の", "s": 0.613, "e": 0.725, "sm": 612, "em": 725, "cs": 4, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "マドリード", "s": 0.738, "e": 1.275, "sm": 737, "em": 1275, "cs": 5, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "で", "s": 1.288, "e": 1.55, "sm": 1287, "em": 1550, "cs": 10, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "、", "s": 1.55, "e": 1.812, "sm": 1550, "em": 1812, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "87", "s": 1.812, "e": 2.438, "sm": 1812, "em": 2437, "cs": 12, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "歳", "s": 2.438, "e": 2.75, "sm": 2437, "em": 2750, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "の", "s": 2.763, "e": 2.875, "sm": 2762, "em": 2875, "cs": 15, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "マリカルメン", "s": 2.888, "e": 3.562, "sm": 2887, "em": 3562, "cs": 16, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "・", "s": 3.562, "e": 3.837, "sm": 3562, "em": 3837, "cs": 22, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "アバスカル", "s": 3.837, "e": 4.425, "sm": 3837, "em": 4425, "cs": 23, "ce": 28, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "さん", "s": 4.438, "e": 4.638, "sm": 4437, "em": 4637, "cs": 28, "ce": 30, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "が", "s": 4.65, "e": 4.763, "sm": 4650, "em": 4762, "cs": 30, "ce": 31, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "亡くなり", "s": 4.775, "e": 5.263, "sm": 4775, "em": 5262, "cs": 31, "ce": 35, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": "まし", "s": 5.275